  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656470",
      "title": "TD: Adding Validation to check User Input",
      "lectureOrder": 515,
      "videoOrder": 472,
      "sourceHash": "5f7b425479cdae1160a074e5b9718ef6dc232d902059fb29a038ab74432812f9",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.31,
          "end": 4.47,
          "en": "-: So, as mentioned at the end of the last lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.47,
          "end": 7.59,
          "en": "Would be nice if we could validate the user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.59,
          "end": 10.68,
          "en": "Something very important in any app you build.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.68,
          "end": 13.92,
          "en": "Whilst you should still validate input on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.92,
          "end": 16.56,
          "en": "as the front, and can always be tricked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.56,
          "end": 18.93,
          "en": "you can greatly enhance user experience,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.93,
          "end": 21.36,
          "en": "by also validating the input here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.36,
          "end": 23.07,
          "en": "For example, you want to make sure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.07,
          "end": 25.92,
          "en": "that none of the fields here is empty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.92,
          "end": 27.33,
          "en": "and that the email address,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.33,
          "end": 29.94,
          "en": "actually is a valid email address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.94,
          "end": 33.96,
          "en": "So, let's go back to our app component, to the HTML file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.96,
          "end": 38.43,
          "en": "to the template, and see how we can add such validators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.43,
          "end": 40.74,
          "en": "Now, since we use the template driven approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.74,
          "end": 43.77,
          "en": "We can only add them in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.77,
          "end": 45.66,
          "en": "And here we can, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.66,
          "end": 48.78,
          "en": "add \"required\" to our username input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.78,
          "end": 52.62,
          "en": "Now, \"required\" is a default HTML attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.62,
          "end": 54.6,
          "en": "You can add to a input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.6,
          "end": 58.11,
          "en": "Here, However, Angular will detect it, so it acts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.11,
          "end": 61.95,
          "en": "as a selector for a built indirective shipping with Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.95,
          "end": 66.39,
          "en": "And it will automatically configure your form you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.39,
          "end": 67.77,
          "en": "to take this into account.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.77,
          "end": 72.36,
          "en": "To make sure that now, this will be treated as invalid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.36,
          "end": 75,
          "en": "if, well, it is empty.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75,
          "end": 77.43,
          "en": "And on the email, we can for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.43,
          "end": 80.43,
          "en": "therefore, also add, \"required\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.43,
          "end": 85.28999999999999,
          "en": "And there also is a email directive you can add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.28999999999999,
          "end": 88.17,
          "en": "Now, email is not a built-in HTML attribute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.17,
          "end": 89.55,
          "en": "It still is a directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.55,
          "end": 92.58,
          "en": "And keep in mind, required is only treated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.58,
          "end": 95.61,
          "en": "as a selector for a angular directive here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.61,
          "end": 98.75999999999999,
          "en": "And email is simply another directive made available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.75999999999999,
          "end": 101.94,
          "en": "by Angler, which makes sure that this is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.94,
          "end": 104.52000000000001,
          "en": "actually a valid email address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.52000000000001,
          "end": 107.19,
          "en": "So, now if we save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.19,
          "end": 110.55,
          "en": "and we have a look at our form here, and I submit it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.55,
          "end": 112.56,
          "en": "I can still submit it, because we haven't set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.56,
          "end": 115.47,
          "en": "up anything which would prevent us from doing so.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.47,
          "end": 118.47,
          "en": "But if we have a look at it and check the valid attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 118.47,
          "end": 120.63,
          "en": "you see it as false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.63,
          "end": 124.59,
          "en": "And if I enter something here, I enter something here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.59,
          "end": 128.46,
          "en": "So, it's filled, but the email address is still not valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.46,
          "end": 131.76,
          "en": "You see, that's still valid as false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.76,
          "end": 134.94,
          "en": "Only, if I turn this into a valid email address here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.94,
          "end": 136.74,
          "en": "only in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.74,
          "end": 140.57999999999998,
          "en": "Now, if we submit it, now you see valid as true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.57999999999998,
          "end": 143.67000000000002,
          "en": "So now, Angler tracks the state of this form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 143.67000000000002,
          "end": 145.23,
          "en": "and correctly informs us,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 145.23,
          "end": 147.57,
          "en": "or gives us a chance of querying it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 147.57,
          "end": 150.24,
          "en": "Whether this form is valid or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 150.24,
          "end": 153.66,
          "en": "And actually this does not only work on form level.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 153.66,
          "end": 156.27,
          "en": "If we dive into the actual controls.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 156.27,
          "end": 158.46,
          "en": "You see that on the email control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 158.46,
          "end": 163.05,
          "en": "We also have a valid attribute, which is true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 163.05,
          "end": 166.65,
          "en": "So, it tracks this on a per-control level,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 166.65,
          "end": 169.95,
          "en": "and then also on a form level.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 169.95,
          "end": 174.69,
          "en": "Now, there also, is a number of place where it tracks this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.69,
          "end": 176.28,
          "en": "and helps us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 176.28,
          "end": 181.28,
          "en": "If we inspect this email element here, in the HTML code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 181.65,
          "end": 184.41,
          "en": "You see, that it adds a couple of classes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 184.41,
          "end": 187.29,
          "en": "because the form control class here is by us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.29,
          "end": 189.87,
          "en": "It's a bootstrap class to give it some styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 189.87,
          "end": 193.44,
          "en": "But, ng dirty, ng touched and ng valid?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.44,
          "end": 195.54,
          "en": "these are not classes added by us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195.54,
          "end": 197.94,
          "en": "And the ng at the beginning makes it pretty clear,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 197.94,
          "end": 201.9,
          "en": "who is responsible for adding these classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 201.9,
          "end": 203.94,
          "en": "Now watch these classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 203.94,
          "end": 207.06,
          "en": "If I remove the @ sign here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 207.06,
          "end": 208.17000000000002,
          "en": "you saw that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 208.17000000000002,
          "end": 212.7,
          "en": "ng invalid was added, and ng valid was removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 212.7,
          "end": 216.21,
          "en": "So, Angler dynamically adds some classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 216.21,
          "end": 218.88,
          "en": "Giving us information, some CSS classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 218.88,
          "end": 221.04,
          "en": "Giving us information about the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 221.04,
          "end": 223.32,
          "en": "of the individual control here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 223.32,
          "end": 224.91,
          "en": "whether it is dirty or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 224.91,
          "end": 228.21,
          "en": "So, whether we did change the initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 228.21,
          "end": 230.01,
          "en": "whether it is touched, or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 230.01,
          "end": 232.14,
          "en": "So, whether we clicked into it, or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 232.14,
          "end": 234.18,
          "en": "And whether it is valid, or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 234.18,
          "end": 236.43,
          "en": "Now, with that information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 236.43,
          "end": 239.37,
          "en": "We can style these inputs conditionally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 239.37,
          "end": 242.49,
          "en": "So, let's the next lecture take advantage of the fact,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 242.49,
          "end": 245.01,
          "en": "that Angler tracks the state of the validity,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 245.01,
          "end": 246.78,
          "en": "and of the form overall.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 246.78,
          "end": 248.91,
          "en": "And change the styling and the behavior,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 248.91,
          "end": 251.673,
          "en": "the user experience with that form.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
